* Test git gq backup
---------------------------------------

$ git gq pop
HEAD is now at abcdef0 script.sh was improved.

$ git gq applied
abcdef0 script.sh was improved.
abcdef0 README was improved.

$ git gq unapplied
README-was-extended.patch

$ git gq backup
Initialized empty Git repository in /.gqpatches/.git/
[master (root-commit) abcdef0] backup 2001-12-31T091234
6 files changed, 63 insertions(+)
create mode 100644 default/README-was-extended.patch
create mode 100644 default/applied/0001-README-was-improved.patch
create mode 100644 default/applied/0002-script.sh-was-improved.patch
create mode 100644 default/parent
create mode 100644 default/series
create mode 100644 queue
.gqpatches/default/applied/0001-README-was-improved.patch
.gqpatches/default/applied/0002-script.sh-was-improved.patch

Created backup:
$ git gq qrepo log -- --oneline | cat
abcdef0 backup 2001-12-31T091234

Now create an extra, new file, 'NEW_FILE':
$ git add NEW_FILE
$ git commit -m 'NEW_FILE added'
[master abcdef0] NEW_FILE added
1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
create mode 100644 NEW_FILE

$ git gq applied
abcdef0 NEW_FILE added
abcdef0 script.sh was improved.
abcdef0 README was improved.

$ git gq unapplied
README-was-extended.patch

Now revert the patch queue directly:
$ git gq revert
